# Agent work lifecycle

Managed path from prompt to durable handoff. Purpose: **stop human-drift and edit spirals** — discovery once, Plan before Build, close with a handoff that the next session can resume.

```text
Prompt → Classify → [Simple: edit+verify] | [Planned: Bootstrap → Plan → Approve → Build → Verify → Deploy notes → Handoff] → Iterate
```

## 1) Classify

| Kind | Criteria | Plan required? |
|------|----------|----------------|
| **Simple** | Copy/typo; roughly one file; no schema/API contract change; no deploy/runbook; no cross-repo; answer already visible in open code or a tiny config toggle with no behavior risk | No |
| **Planned** | Needs local knowledge lookup (blueprint / handoffs / prior art / index), **or** more than a simple edit, **or** write-path / migration / multi-file behavior change, **or** unclear architecture | **Yes — always** |

When unsure, treat as **Planned**.

## 2) Planned work — HARD-GATE

<HARD-GATE>
For **Planned** work: run [agent-context-bootstrap.mdc](agent-context-bootstrap.mdc) → **create a Plan** → **no Build file edits** until approved (or the user already said build/approve/go *and* the Plan was still produced first in this turn / Plan mode).
</HARD-GATE>

### Plan must include

- **Scope** — repo(s) / paths in play
- **Bootstrap citations** — blueprint path; key handoff(s); prior-art hits reused or “none”
- **Approach** — what changes and why (not a novel)
- **Verify** — exact test command and/or one manual smoke
- **Deploy truth** — pointer to blueprint Deployment section (or n/a)
- **Follow-up / resume** — what the next session should pick up

Write-path / save-load / schema work: also complete the vertical-slice checklist when that workspace rule exists, **inside the Plan** before edits.

### Approval

Do not start Build until one of:

- User says build / approve / go / implement the plan
- Saved plan status moves to `in_queue` or `in_progress` ([plans-management.mdc](plans-management.mdc) when present)
- Prompt already ordered implement-now **and** the agent still created the Plan before editing

If approval is unclear → stay in Plan mode / ask; do not silently code.

## 3) Execute (Build)

- Stay inside [workspace-repo-scope.mdc](workspace-repo-scope.mdc)
- Run the **Verify** steps from the Plan before treating work as done
- Do not expand scope without updating the Plan (re-approve if material)

## 4) Close

1. **`handoff_write`** — full artifact (decisions, files, verify results, Follow-up). Never edit handoff files directly.
2. **Chat** — short summary + markdown link to the handoff path ([handoff-logging.mdc](handoff-logging.mdc))
3. **`## Deployment`** — copy-paste host CLI when deployable or host commands were given; else `## Deployment (n/a)`
4. Saved plan used → set status `done` when complete

## 5) Iterate (no rediscovery)

| Situation | Action |
|-----------|--------|
| Same Agent tab | Append handoff `## iN`; continue from prior decisions |
| New tab / later day | `knowledge_recent` + read last **Follow-up** / latest `## iN` **before** re-walking the codebase; cite that handoff in the new Plan |
| First failure after a change | **Stop coding.** Re-check request contract / DB / assumptions; update Plan or handoff with assumption vs reality; then edit. No tip-of-iceberg patches. |

## Relationship to other gates

| Gate | Role |
|------|------|
| [agent-context-bootstrap.mdc](agent-context-bootstrap.mdc) | DB-first discovery before Plan/Build |
| [prior-art.mdc](prior-art.mdc) | Graph/FTS before designing |
| [blueprints.mdc](blueprints.mdc) | Architecture + deploy map |
| [handoff-logging.mdc](handoff-logging.mdc) | Close + resume payload |
| [plans-management.mdc](plans-management.mdc) | Saved plan folders/status (when present) |
| Vertical-slice / Linear / commit rules | Workspace overlays when present — run **inside** this lifecycle, not instead of it |

Order for Planned work: **bootstrap → (vertical-slice if write-path) → Plan → approve → Build → verify → deploy notes → handoff → iterate**.
